# Porthleven: a harbour town, and mua's main World Definition.
#
# Newcomers step off the ferry onto the Harbour Steps. From there the town
# runs north up the High Street to The Ship, a chandler's shop, the
# lighthouse keeper's walled garden and the headland, where a causeway
# crosses to the lighthouse when the tide is out.
#
# The lighthouse has been dark since a storm, and its keeper, Ezra
# Trethewey, is missing. Following that thread takes a player through most
# of what mua can do, but nothing in the town is reachable only through it.
#
# Each district is its own file, with its Scripts in `scripts/<district>/`:
#
#   town.edl         the atoms, component definitions and Verbs every district shares
#   quay.edl         the Harbour Steps, fish market, slipway, boatyard, and the sea
#   high-street.edl  the square, the chandler's shop and Hill Lane
#   ship.edl         The Ship, its bar and back room
#   headland.edl     the headland, the lighthouse and its lamp room
#   garden.edl       the keeper's walled garden, orchard, well and shed
#
# The Starting room is `harbour_steps`.

include "mua-scripts:edl/base.edl"

include "town.edl"
include "quay.edl"
include "high-street.edl"
include "ship.edl"
include "headland.edl"
include "garden.edl"
